    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0601" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg517"/>

                <head>No. 265.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodbury to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Boston</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 30, 1886</date>.
                        [Received July 31.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith is transmitted the affidavit of
                    the crew of the schooner Thomas F. Bayard, relative to her having been forced to
                    abandon her fishing voyage on the northwest coast of Newfoundland, and return
                    home, in consequence of a warning that she would be seized by the shore
                    authorities if she fished or bought bait within the three-mile limit, which has
                    been transmitted to the Department. My information is that the schooner has
                    sailed on another trip.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHAS. LEVI WOODBURY.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d269-a1.xml" xpointer="d269-a1"/>
